WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.720
- After surviving breast cancer,

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:05.070
our next guest has made it her mission

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:08.120
to make major strides, literally,

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.490
in raising money and awareness

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.600
to fight this horrible disease.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.770
Sharael Kolberg is running 50 miles

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:18.050
for 50 days in 50 states,

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.830
all in the name of finding a cure.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.210
And Sharael joins me now.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:26.041
Hi, Sharael!
- Hi, Drew.

00:00:26.041 --> 00:00:28.150
Hi, thank you so much for having me.

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.610
I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:32.720
- Oh, Sharael, we really
wanted to make a whole segment

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.160
out of this because I was
blown away by your story.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.350
So much so, there's just
a lot to talk about.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:41.530
How are you feeling now?

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:43.130
What's your latest diagnosis?

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:44.303
How is everything?

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.410
- I'm doing great.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:50.090
I have been cancer-free
since last December.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:52.557
Doing great, living life, yeah.

00:00:52.557 --> 00:00:55.590
Living every day to the
moment, so it's awesome.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:57.140
- Oh, that's so wonderful.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:01.090
You really are an inspiration
in every single aspect

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:06.090
of life, health and wellness,
mental space, philanthropy.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:10.520
And what sort of was the
running piece of the puzzle?

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:12.283
What made that click for you?

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:14.900
- Well, I've always been a runner,

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.260
and when I was going through treatment

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:18.500
there were days when I literally

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:20.320
could not even get out of bed.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.980
So for me, it was really
important to get back to running,

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.760
to make me feel normal again.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:29.200
And it's a great way
to get people involved

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.650
and promote breast cancer awareness

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:33.400
and give people hope.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.380
So it's been great.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.550
I love running, and it's
a great way to get out,

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:40.220
get exercise, mental
health, physical health.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:41.053
It's all good.

00:01:41.053 --> 00:01:45.580
- I will say that you have
truly incentivized here.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.470
Sometimes, you know, we don't really know

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:49.710
how to get involved,

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:52.870
and the way that you've
presented your website

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:55.283
and the challenge, I scoured through it,

00:01:56.296 --> 00:01:59.990
I am very excited to
try to join you on this.

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:02.360
But first I have a very
exciting announcement.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:05.143
I would like to introduce someone to you.

00:02:05.143 --> 00:02:06.610
- Okay.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:08.780
- So we all think what you're doing here

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:11.190
is just so important, and this is Jill

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:15.035
from none other than, get ready
for this, Bank of America.

00:02:15.035 --> 00:02:16.713
(audience clapping)
(audience cheering)

00:02:16.713 --> 00:02:18.800
Drop the mic.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.890
Jill, thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:24.140
Why is it important for
you to be here today?

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:26.890
- Thank you, Drew.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:29.200
Thank you for having me,
it's so great to be here.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.840
And Sharael, my colleagues
and I at Bank of America

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.100
have been following your story,

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:38.520
and we're so impressed by all
the work that you're doing

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.260
and the commitment that you've made

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:43.070
to raise awareness around breast cancer

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:45.220
and give so much hope to so many.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:50.140
So to thank you for
running 50 miles in 50 days

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:53.490
with partners across 50 states,

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:58.490
in your honor, we're gonna
donate $50,000 to Susan G. Komen.

00:02:58.930 --> 00:02:59.763
- Oh, my god.

00:02:59.763 --> 00:03:00.742
(Drew screaming)
(Drew clapping)

00:03:00.742 --> 00:03:01.841
Are you serious?

00:03:01.841 --> 00:03:04.670
That's amazing, thank you so much.

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:06.850
You're gonna help save so many lives.

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.260
That is amazing.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.980
- You know what?
- I can't thank you enough.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:11.910
- Actually, that's not all.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:14.470
Jill, is there something else?

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:15.540
- [Sharael] What?

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.020
- There's just one more thing.

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:20.620
I mean, this year has
just been so unprecedented

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:25.270
in so many ways, and your
story is even more inspiring,

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:28.030
and in the hopes that one
day no one has to face

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:29.930
a breast cancer diagnosis alone,

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:34.670
so in celebration of your
50th-birthday milestone,

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:39.670
we're gonna donate another
$50,000 for a total of $100,000.

00:03:39.851 --> 00:03:42.787
- That's $100,000!
(audience clapping)

00:03:44.259 --> 00:03:45.700
- Thank you so much.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:48.680
That means so much to me
and for all those women

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:50.890
that are battling this terrible disease,

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:52.360
you're gonna help find a cure.

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:53.800
Thank you so much.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:56.100
- And Jill, I cannot thank you enough

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.760
for this incredible opportunity.

00:03:57.760 --> 00:03:59.160
You are our hero.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.520
And, Sharael, you have inspired me.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.070
I'm gonna post the website on our site.

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:05.280
I'm joining you.

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.720
I'm gonna try to run the
mile by October 31st.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:11.060
October is Breast Cancer Awareness Month,

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:14.690
and so in honor of you, our pod, our squad

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:16.030
is gonna start the mission.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:17.940
We're gonna start a Facebook group,

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.990
and we wanna do this with you.

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:21.700
I've never run a mile in my life.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:22.533
I'm so excited.

00:04:22.533 --> 00:04:24.611
- Thank you.
- Everybody get involved.

00:04:24.611 --> 00:04:27.194
(upbeat music)

